# oracle: pair_style pace with the .yace potential of the LAMMPS example PACKAGES/apip (Cu-1.yace: ChebPow radial basis, FinnisSinclairShiftedScaled embedding, density inner cutoff) on a 3x3x3 fcc Cu cell with displaced atoms, 300 K NVE, 30 steps
# Native reference: LAMMPS b332f28 built with PKG_ML-PACE (the installed binary has no ML-PACE; see w257pace_recursive)
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 8.8e-15, atoms 6.6e-15.
# oracle-examples: PACKAGES/apip/Cu-1.yace
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all
units       metal
atom_style  atomic
lattice     fcc 3.6
region      box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box  1 box
create_atoms 1 box
mass        1 63.546
displace_atoms all random 0.1 0.1 0.1 8812 units box
velocity    all create 300 4928459 rot yes dist gaussian
pair_style  pace
pair_coeff  * * Cu-1.yace Cu
fix         1 all nve
timestep    0.001
thermo_style custom step temp pe ke etotal press pxy
thermo_modify format float %.15g
thermo      5
run         30
